, 23:32, 24:50, 25:32, 26:50, 27:80, 28:20, 29:32, 30:50, 31:32, 32:50, 33:80, 34:32, 35:50, 36:80\n\nqmin1_50 (G100:3, G160:5, G250:8, G400:12.5, G650:20, G1000:32, G1600:50):\n1:3, 2:5, 3:8, 4:3, 5:5, 6:8, 7:5, 8:8, 9:12.5, 10:3, 11:5, 12:8, 13:5, 14:8, 15:12.5, 16:12.5, 17:20, 18:32, 19:5, 20:8, 21:12.5, 22:12.5, 23:20, 24:32, 25:20, 26:32, 27:50, 28:12.5, 29:20, 30:32, 31:20, 32:32, 33:50, 34:20, 35:32, 36:50\n\nOK. Now also blade_angle, blade_qty, control_element, number_of_drums, bearings — put in matrix_tables rows (they're in the rows anyway). Should I also do model_level for them? To keep JSON size manageable, no — they're fully captured in matrix_tables. The rules emphasize varying attributes → model_level, but matrix_tables explicitly \"preserve multi-dim tables that don't fit elsewhere\". The blade/bearing/drums attributes fit in the matrix table. I'll keep model_level to the flow rates (matching the R137 example pattern).\n\nHmm, but control_element and number_of_drums also vary by model (G1000+ rows have 8/0 and 0.2). They're in the matrix rows, so preserved. I think that's acceptable.\n\nmatrix_tables description: \"Main characteristics, essential characteristics, conditional parts and essential parts of FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx and FMT-Dc turbine gas meters by type, DN and G-value. Qmin columns are given per meter ratio (MR) with applicable pressure ranges: MR 1:20 for 0..101 bar(g), MR 1:30 for 4..101 bar(g), MR 1:50 for 8..101 bar(g). Bearing dimensions are inside diameter x outside diameter x width in mm; standard bearings for 0..101 bar(g), optional bearings for 4..101 bar(g).\"\n\nShould I add footnote-like info? No footnotes present.\n\nAlso, first table (page 2) \"Table 1: FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx and FMT-Dc\" — general characteristics. Should that be a matrix_table too? It's key-value; extracted as type_level characteristics. I'll not duplicate it as matrix_table. Hmm, but there are two \"Table 1\" names (page 2 general, page 3 main matrix). I'll name the page-3 table \"Main characteristics and essential parts (Table on page 3)\". Fine.\n\nFor certified_type description: \"A turbine gas meter\" → \"Turbine gas meter\". \n\nNow certificate.scheme: The OIML-CS has scheme A for certificates of conformity. I'll set \"A\".\n\nLet me also double check \"control element\" unit: the units row gives m³/h for control element column. Values 0,02 → 0.02 and 0,2 → 0.2, unit m³/h.\n\nNumber of drums: \"7 / 1\" and \"8 / 0\" — string.\n\nBearing dims strings: \"3x6x3\", \"2x5x2\", \"3x8x4\", \"3x6x3\", \"5x10x3\", \"5x11x5\", \"5x16x5\", \"8x22x7\".\n\nBlade angle degree: 55, 45, 35. Blade qty: 12, 14, 16.\n\nNow assemble rows. I'll write them compactly. Each row object:\n\n{model_id, type, dn_body, dn_cartridge, g_value, qmax, qt, qmin_meter_ratio_1_20, qmin_meter_ratio_1_30, qmin_meter_ratio_1_50, number_of_drums, control_element, blade_angle, blade_quantity, bearing_front_standard, bearing_rear_standard, bearing_front_optional, bearing_rear_optional}\n\nGroup 1 rows (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 50, 80; drums \"7 / 1\"; control 0.02; bearings 3x6x3, 2x5x2, 3x8x4, 3x6x3):\nr1: G100: 160, 32, 8, 5, 3, 55, 12\nr2: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 45, 14\nr3: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 35, 16\n\nGroup 2 (FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 80, 80; same drums/control/bearings as G1):\nr4: G100: 160, 32, 8, 5, 3, 55, 12\nr5: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 45, 14\nr6: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 35, 16\n\nGroup 3 (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 80, 100; drums 7/1; control 0.02; bearings 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 5x10x3, 3x6x3):\nr7: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 55, 12\nr8: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 45, 14\nr9: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 35, 16\n\nGroup 4 (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 100, 80; drums 7/1; control 0.02; bearings 3x6x3, 2x5x2, 3x8x4, 3x6x3):\nr10: G100: 160, 32, 8, 5, 3, 55, 12\nr11: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 45, 14\nr12: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 35, 16\n\nGroup 5 (all, 100, 100; drums 7/1; control 0.02; bearings 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 5x10x3, 3x6x3):\nr13: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 55, 12\nr14: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 45, 14\nr15: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 35, 16\n\nGroup 6 (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 100, 150; bearings 5x11x5, 5x11x5, 5x16x5, 5x11x5):\nr16: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5; drums 7/1, control 0.02; blade 55, 12\nr17: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20; drums 7/1, control 0.02; blade 45, 14\nr18: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32; drums 8/0, control 0.2; blade 35, 16\n\nGroup 7 (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 150, 100; drums 7/1; control 0.02; bearings 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 5x10x3, 3x6x3):\nr19: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 55, 12\nr20: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 45, 14\nr21: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 35, 16\n\nGroup 8 (all, 150, 150; bearings 5x11x5, 5x11x5, 5x16x5, 5x11x5):\nr22: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5; 7/1, 0.02; 55, 12\nr23: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20; 7/1, 0.02; 45, 14\nr24: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32; 8/0, 0.2; 35, 16\n\nGroup 9 (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 150, 200; bearings 5x16x5, 5x16x5, 8x22x7, 5x16x5):\nr25: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20; 7/1, 0.02; 55, 12\nr26: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32; 8/0, 0.2; 45, 14\nr27: G1600: 2500, 500, 125, 80, 50; 8/0, 0.2; 35, 16\n\nGroup 10 (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 200, 150; bearings 5x11x5, 5x11x5, 5x16x5, 5x11x5):\nr28: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5; 7/1, 0.02; 55, 12\nr29: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20; 7/1, 0.02; 45, 14\nr30: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32; 8/0, 0.2; 35, 16\n\nGroup 11 (all, 200, 200; bearings 5x16x5, 5x16x5, 8x22x7, 5x16x5):\nr31: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20; 7/1, 0.02; 55, 12\nr32: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32; 8/0, 0.2; 45, 14\nr33: G1600: 2500, 500, 125, 80, 50; 8/0, 0.2; 35, 16\n\nGroup 12 (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 250, 200; bearings 5x16x5, 5x16x5, 8x22x7, 5x16x5):\nr34: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20; 7/1, 0.02; 55, 12\nr35: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32; 8/0, 0.2; 45, 14\nr36: G1600: 2500, 500, 125, 80, 50; 8/0, 0.2; 35, 16\n\nNow the JSON. This will be long but let me write it carefully.\n\nAlso the models[] entries. 36 entries with model_id, label, attributes. Let me write label as e.g. \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, DN 50 body / 80 cartridge, G 100\". Attributes: {type: [\"FMT-Lx\",\"FMT-Dc\"] or all four, dn_body_mm: 50, dn_cartridge_mm: 80, g_value: 100}.\n\nHmm — should type in attributes be a list? Yes, since group says \"or\". Fine.\n\nShould I include qmax etc. in model attributes too? Redundant with model_level; skip.\n\nCertificate-level: also \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\" — from \"OIML Issuing Authority NL1\". \n\nLet me also double-check accuracy class: \"Accuracy class 1\" — so accuracy_classes: [\"1\"]. Could also write [1]. Keep [\"1\"]? Hmm, numeric might be fine. The class is \"1\". I'll use [\"1\"].\n\nEdition: R 137-1 (2012) — edition 2012. amendment: null — omit or null? I'll set amendment: null.\n\nNow regarding revision_history: I'm slightly torn. The header says \"revision 1\" — I'll include:\n\"revision_history\": [{\"revision\": \"1\", \"date\": \"2015-07-31\", \"changes\": null}]\n\nOK. Config-level entries: I defined two. Also maybe a third config axis: control element? No — that varies by model, in matrix.\n\nNow the type_level characteristics: also add \"documentation_folder\" — no, that's in test_reports.\n\nAlso \"destined for measurement\" — I'll label it \"measured_quantity\": {value: \"Gas volume\"}.\n\nLet me now also consider whether the general Table 1 should be a matrix_table named \"General characteristics\". It's not multi-dimensional; type_level suffices. Skip.\n\nWrite the final JSON. Keys order: certificate, issuing_authority, applicants, manufacturers, certified_type, model_family, characteristics, matrix_tables, recommendation, test_reports, revision_history.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nFor unit_id: leave null everywhere (per rule 3). Should I include unit_id key at all? The schema shape includes it. I'll include \"unit_id\": null in type_level values, and at model_level attribute level include unit_symbol only (following the example, values don't carry unit). For model_level entries the example: {\"attribute\": \"qmax\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"G1.6\", \"value\": 2.5}]} — no unit_id. I'll include unit_id: null there too? The example didn't. I'll follow the example and omit unit_id at model_level, but include at type_level? For consistency, maybe include unit_id: null everywhere in type_level, and in config_level values. Eh — I'll include \"unit_id\": null in type_level and config_level; model_level keep like example (attribute-level unit_symbol only). Actually to be safe and consistent, add unit_id: null at attribute level for model_level too. The example doesn't show it but adding null shouldn't hurt. Hmm, keep it minimal per example: attribute, unit_symbol, values. I'll add unit_id: null anyway for schema conformance. Fine.\n\nBearing dims unit \"mm\" — but values are composite strings \"3x6x3\". Unit mm applies.\n\nNow double-check some numbers from the markdown:\n\nGroup 1 row1: `<td>100</td><td>160</td><td>32</td><td>8</td><td>5</td><td>3</td>` — G100, Qmax160, Qt32, Qmin 8/5/3. blade 55, 12. ✓\n\nRow2: 160, 250, 50, 12,5, 8, 5 → G160, 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5; blade 45, 14 ✓\nRow3: 250, 400, 80, 20, 12,5, 8 → G250, 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8; blade 35, 16 ✓\n\nGroup 3: 160→250,50,12.5,8,5; 250→400,80,20,12.5,8; 400→650,130,32,5→32.5,20,12,5→12.5 ✓\n\nGroup 6: 400→650,130,32.5,20,12.5; 650→1000,200,50,32,20; 1000→1600,320,80,50,32 ✓\n\nGroup 9: 650→1000,200,50,32,20; 1000→1600,320,80,50,32; 1600→2500,500,125,80,50 ✓\n\nGood.\n\nNow write JSON. It'll be big. Let me be careful with commas and structure.\n\nOne more thought on matrix_tables \"name\": \"Main characteristics and essential parts (Table 1, page 3)\". Actually page 3 table header just says \"Table 1\" too. Name: \"Main characteristics, essential characteristics, conditional parts and essential parts\". Keep simpler: \"Main characteristics and essential parts by type, DN and G-value\".\n\nDescription should capture the sub-headers: Qmin per meter ratio MR 1:20/1:30/1:50 with pressure ranges; bearing dims front/rear standard (0..101 bar(g)) and optional (4..101 bar(g)); number of drums before/after decimal point; control element value in m³/h.\n\nAlso, matrix_tables \"footnotes\": [] — omit since empty.\n\nLet me write the final answer now.\n\nAlso should I include \"components\"? I decided no. Hmm, but rule 6 and the table explicitly labels \"1.1 Essential parts\" (blade, bearings) and \"1.4 Conditional parts\" (drums, control element). Adding components with role \"essential_part\" and type_designations like \"Blade\", \"Ball bearing\" — the bearing dims vary by model. I could add components:\n\n- {role: \"essential_part\", type_designations: [\"Blade\"], characteristics: {}}? Empty characteristics is noise. I'll skip components — the data lives in matrix_tables. That's defensible: the fragment names part categories but the per-model characteristics are in the matrix.\n\nActually, let me reconsider adding a bearing component with alternatives: standard bearings OR optional bearings (alternatives \"OR\") with pressure applicability. That's a genuine config alternative:\n\ncomponents: [\n  {\n    \"role\": \"bearing\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"Standard bearing\", \"Optional bearing\"],\n    \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n    \"characteristics\": {\n      \"applicable_pressure_range_standard\": {...}, \n    }\n  }\n]\n\nHmm, this is getting speculative about naming. The cert doesn't name bearing types beyond \"standard bearings\"/\"optional bearings\". I could add one component entry:\n\n{\"role\": \"essential_part\", \"type_designations\": [\"Ball bearings (front and rear)\"], \"alternatives\": \"OR\", \"characteristics\": {\"standard_bearings_pressure_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\":0,\"max\":101}, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar(g)\"}, \"optional_bearings_pressure_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\":4,\"max\":101}, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar(g)\"}}, note dimensions per model in matrix}\n\n\"Ball\" is fabricated — they're just \"bearings\". I'll do:\n\ncomponents: [\n  {\n    \"role\": \"essential_part_bearing\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"standard bearings\", \"optional bearings\"],\n    \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n    \"characteristics\": {\n      \"dimensions_format\": \"inside diameter x outside diameter x width\",\n      \"dimensions_unit\": \"mm\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nEh. I think it adds interpretive noise. The instruction: \"include ONLY if cert names sub-assemblies\". It does name them. But per-model values live in the matrix. I'll include a light components entry for bearings and one for the control element/drums? Hmm.\n\nLet me just include bearings as a component with alternatives OR and characteristics describing format + pressure applicability, since that's genuinely structured:\n\n{\n  \"role\": \"essential_part\",\n  \"type_designations\": [\"standard bearings\", \"optional bearings\"],\n  \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"dimension_notation\": \"inside diameter x outside diameter x width\",\n    \"standard_bearings_pressure_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0, \"max\": 101}, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar(g)\", \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []},\n    \"optional_bearings_pressure_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 4, \"max\": 101}, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar(g)\", \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n  }\n}\n\nHmm, footnote_markers empty — omit. I'll include this component. And skip control element/blades components (purely per-model values in matrix). Actually, I worry about over-engineering. Let me keep components with just the bearing entry. Actually you know, I'll skip components entirely — the \"standard/optional bearings\" are columns in the matrix, captured with their pressure conditions in config_level and matrix description. Simpler and less fabricated. Final: no components[].\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider once more. Rule 6 example: \"Measuring sensor FM01 + Pulser P2 + Calculating device WB\" — those are named sub-assemblies with type designations. Here bearings have no type designations, just dimensions. Blades have angle/qty. The control element has values. These are characteristics, not named sub-assemblies. Skipping components is fine.\n\nNow, output. Writing the full JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R137/2012-NL1-14.03\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"project_number\": \"SO15202424\",\n    \"page_total\": 5,\n    \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2015-07-31\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"NMi Certin B.V.\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Hugo de Grootplein 1\", \"3314 EG Dordrecht\", \"the Netherlands\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"C. Oosterman\",\n    \"person_title\": \"Head Certification Board\",\n    \"phone\": \"+31 78 6332332\",\n    \"email\": \"certin@nmi.nl\",\n    \"website\": \"www.nmi.nl\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Flow Meter Group B.V.\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Meniststraat 5c\", \"7091 ZZ Dinxperlo\", \"The Netherlands\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Flow Meter Group B.V.\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Meniststraat 5c\", \"7091 ZZ Dinxperlo\", \"The Netherlands\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Gas meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"FMT-L\", \"FMT-S\", \"FMT-Lx\", \"FMT-Dc\"],\n    \"description\": \"Turbine gas meter\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"FMT\",\n    \"models\": [ ... 36 ... ]\n  },\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {...},\n    \"model_level\": [...],\n    \"config_level\": [...]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [ ... ],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R137\",\n    \"edition\": 2012,\n    \"amendment\": null,\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [\"1\"]\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [...],\n  \"revision_history\": [{\"revision\": \"1\", \"date\": \"2015-07-31\", \"changes\": null}]\n}\n\nShould amendment be included as null? \"Don't fabricate\" — amendment null is fine (explicitly no amendment mentioned). I'll include null.\n\nNow writing the 36 model entries:\n\n1 {\"model_id\": \"DN50/80-G100\", \"label\": \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, DN body 50, DN cartridge 80, G 100\", \"attributes\": {\"type\": [\"FMT-Lx\", \"FMT-Dc\"], \"dn_body_mm\": 50, \"dn_cartridge_mm\": 80, \"g_value\": 100}}\n2 {\"model_id\": \"DN50/80-G160\", ..., \"g_value\": 160}\n3 {\"model_id\": \"DN50/80-G250\", ..., 250}\n4 {\"model_id\": \"DN80/80-G100\", \"label\": \"FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, DN body 80, DN cartridge 80, G 100\", \"attributes\": {\"type\": [\"FMT-L\",\"FMT-S\",\"FMT-Lx\",\"FMT-Dc\"], \"dn_body_mm\": 80, \"dn_cartridge_mm\": 80, \"g_value\": 100}}\n5 DN80/80-G160\n6 DN80/80-G250\n7 {\"model_id\": \"DN80/100-G160\", \"label\": \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, DN body 80, DN cartridge 100, G 160\", attrs Lx/Dc, 80, 100, 160}\n8 DN80/100-G250\n9 DN80/100-G400\n10 DN100/80-G100 (Lx/Dc, 100, 80, 100)\n11 DN100/80-G160\n12 DN100/80-G250\n13 DN100/100-G160 (all, 100, 100, 160)\n14 DN100/100-G250\n15 DN100/100-G400\n16 DN100/150-G400 (Lx/Dc, 100, 150, 400)\n17 DN100/150-G650\n18 DN100/150-G1000\n19 DN150/100-G160 (Lx/Dc, 150, 100, 160)\n20 DN150/100-G250\n21 DN150/100-G400\n22 DN150/150-G400 (all, 150, 150, 400)\n23 DN150/150-G650\n24 DN150/150-G1000\n25 DN150/200-G650 (Lx/Dc, 150, 200, 650)\n26 DN150/200-G1000\n27 DN150/200-G1600\n28 DN200/150-G400 (Lx/Dc, 200, 150, 400)\n29 DN200/150-G650\n30 DN200/150-G1000\n31 DN200/200-G650 (all, 200, 200, 650)\n32 DN200/200-G1000\n33 DN200/200-G1600\n34 DN250/200-G650 (Lx/Dc, 250, 200, 650)\n35 DN250/200-G1000\n36 DN250/200-G1600\n\nOK. Writing it all out now. This is long but let's go.\n\nFor matrix rows I'll write each row fully. Let me draft rows JSON:\n\nr1: {\"model_id\": \"DN50/80-G100\", \"type\": \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", \"dn_body\": 50, \"dn_cartridge\": 80, \"g_value\": 100, \"qmax\": 160, \"qt\": 32, \"qmin_mr_1_20\": 8, \"qmin_mr_1_30\": 5, \"qmin_mr_1_50\": 3, \"number_of_drums\": \"7 / 1\", \"control_element\": 0.02, \"blade_angle\": 55, \"blade_quantity\": 12, \"bearing_front_standard\": \"3x6x3\", \"bearing_rear_standard\": \"2x5x2\", \"bearing_front_optional\": \"3x8x4\", \"bearing_rear_optional\": \"3x6x3\"}\n\nr2: {\"model_id\": \"DN50/80-G160\", \"type\": \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", \"dn_body\": 50, \"dn_cartridge\": 80, \"g_value\": 160, \"qmax\": 250, \"qt\": 50, \"qmin_mr_1_20\": 12.5, \"qmin_mr_1_30\": 8, \"qmin_mr_1_50\": 5, \"number_of_drums\": \"7 / 1\", \"control_element\": 0.02, \"blade_angle\": 45, \"blade_quantity\": 14, \"bearing_front_standard\": \"3x6x3\", \"bearing_rear_standard\": \"2x5x2\", \"bearing_front_optional\": \"3x8x4\", \"bearing_rear_optional\": \"3x6x3\"}\n\nr3: {\"model_id\": \"DN50/80-G250\", ... \"g_value\": 250, \"qmax\": 400, \"qt\": 80, \"qmin_mr_1_20\": 20, \"qmin_mr_1_30\": 12.5, \"qmin_mr_1_50\": 8, ... \"blade_angle\": 35, \"blade_quantity\": 16, bearings same}\n\nr4-r6: DN80/80, type all four.\nr4: G100: 160, 32, 8, 5, 3, 7/1, 0.02, 55, 12, 3x6x3, 2x5x2, 3x8x4, 3x6x3\nr5: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 7/1, 0.02, 45, 14, same bearings\nr6: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 7/1, 0.02, 35, 16, same bearings\n\nr7-r9: DN80/100, Lx/Dc, bearings 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 5x10x3, 3x6x3, drums 7/1, control 0.02\nr7: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 55, 12\nr8: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 45, 14\nr9: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 35, 16\n\nr10-r12: DN100/80, Lx/Dc, bearings 3x6x3, 2x5x2, 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 7/1, 0.02\nr10: G100: 160, 32, 8, 5, 3, 55, 12\nr11: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 45, 14\nr12: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 35, 16\n\nr13-r15: DN100/100, all, bearings 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 5x10x3, 3x6x3, 7/1, 0.02\nr13: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 55, 12\nr14: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 45, 14\nr15: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 35, 16\n\nr16-r18: DN100/150, Lx/Dc, bearings 5x11x5, 5x11x5, 5x16x5, 5x11x5\nr16: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 7/1, 0.02, 55, 12\nr17: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20, 7/1, 0.02, 45, 14\nr18: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32, 8/0, 0.2, 35, 16\n\nr19-r21: DN150/100, Lx/Dc, bearings 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 5x10x3, 3x6x3, 7/1, 0.02\nr19: G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 55, 12\nr20: G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 45, 14\nr21: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 35, 16\n\nr22-r24: DN150/150, all, bearings 5x11x5, 5x11x5, 5x16x5, 5x11x5\nr22: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 7/1, 0.02, 55, 12\nr23: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20, 7/1, 0.02, 45, 14\nr24: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32, 8/0, 0.2, 35, 16\n\nr25-r27: DN150/200, Lx/Dc, bearings 5x16x5, 5x16x5, 8x22x7, 5x16x5\nr25: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20, 7/1, 0.02, 55, 12\nr26: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32, 8/0, 0.2, 45, 14\nr27: G1600: 2500, 500, 125, 80, 50, 8/0, 0.2, 35, 16\n\nr28-r30: DN200/150, Lx/Dc, bearings 5x11x5, 5x11x5, 5x16x5, 5x11x5\nr28: G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 7/1, 0.02, 55, 12\nr29: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20, 7/1, 0.02, 45, 14\nr30: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32, 8/0, 0.2, 35, 16\n\nr31-r33: DN200/200, all, bearings 5x16x5, 5x16x5, 8x22x7, 5x16x5\nr31: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20, 7/1, 0.02, 55, 12\nr32: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32, 8/0, 0.2, 45, 14\nr33: G1600: 2500, 500, 125, 80, 50, 8/0, 0.2, 35, 16\n\nr34-r36: DN250/200, Lx/Dc, bearings 5x16x5, 5x16x5, 8x22x7, 5x16x5\nr34: G650: 1000, 200, 50, 32, 20, 7/1, 0.02, 55, 12\nr35: G1000: 1600, 320, 80, 50, 32, 8/0, 0.2, 45, 14\nr36: G1600: 2500, 500, 125, 80, 50, 8/0, 0.2, 35, 16\n\nmodel_level values arrays — write them per the tables above.\n\nOK, writing final JSON now. I'll be careful about JSON validity (no trailing commas).",
